  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_estell",
      "name": {
        "en": "Estelle's Badge",
        "zh": "艾丝黛尔证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_estell",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Estelle has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for swift and fierce enemy suppression in combat.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Guard Operator during field operations to exercise Centurion responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员艾丝黛尔擅长以凌厉攻势阻击敌人\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为近卫干员，行使强攻手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_estell",
      "name": {
        "en": "Farewell Gifts from the Wildlands",
        "zh": "荒野地的饯别礼",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_estell",
      "description": {
        "en": "'Look at the girl in this photo. Memorize her appearance,' Danny Chip told Rustcage. 'If someone comes to your doorstep with a girl like this, look after her for me.'\nThe careworker at Lloyd Russet Biolaboratories often used to speak with pride, lips pried lightly by alcohol, of how their company had stolen rainforests and headwaters away from the aboriginals that survived on them. Of how amidst crop failure they'd bought the requisite Archosauria children for just twenty gold certificates and a handful of food. He would speak, too, of how those children priced at just twelve bonds would be remodeled into replicas of the 'Archosauria War-God.' At the end of the story, they would defeat their competitors, receive orders from the military, and then come home like kings...\nHalf a year later, the passionate egghead was reduced to a drunkard passing each night with a bottle, always grumbling in despair of the chaos of the experiments: an escaped fowl during Phase II of animal testing, the complete failures of Phases I and II of human testing, all the test subjects destroyed... then ultimately, Subject 75, the most abnormal individual in all the Phase IV human tests.\nSubject 75 was not just devoid of two horns; her personality lacked any resemblance to a weapon of war. Even after provoking her by all proven means, driving her to her last gasp, she showed no hint of the 'War-God' essence at all. Bizarrely, as a failed article, 75 was only a momentary frustration to the careworker. Very quickly, he ceased to drown himself in drink, and began to happily chat with her about daily life, about his wonderful future with Careworker Celina, about how they'd raise a girl that loved princess stories, and go on vacation to Siesta together... A failure, yet one that guided this lost soul back home.\nHowever, all the 'successful' Phase IV subjects suddenly and collectively went out of control during obedience training one day, leading to the deaths of several experiment personnel. As was standard procedure, they had to 'humanely' destroy the subjects of this phase. That evening, Danny came to Rustcage's saloon, and handed him the photograph of Subject 75.\nIn the end, neither Danny nor the girl ever visited that saloon again.\nThe lab later officially declared that Danny had, along with fellow careworker Celina, 'lost their lives together' in the incident.\nSix years later, the noisy saloon patrons have turned into wild hunters, exchanging the saloon's fine dining for the taste of fresh sport... What was once an establishment in the wake of the Great Expansion now exists in solidarity with the Oripathy-blighted and the Pioneers that same wake had cast out unto the dried-up earth. Not even the biolab was spared, resting marooned upon loose rock.\nAt this moment, Rustcage stares at the girl not far away, then looks down to compare the photograph in his hands. He doesn't know why she's grown two big horns, but there's no doubt they're one and the same.\nHe sees the hunt wild and unadulterated, sees the food chain built around her. He sees civilization's mark gradually fading, and the wilderness baring her original face—despite her heavy infection he knows he stands no chance.\nFinally, Rustcage sets down his hunter's crossbow. With the last of his strength, he delivers to her his hoard of oh so many years, these farewell gifts from the wilds.",
        "zh": "“看看照片上的女孩，牢记她的样貌。”丹尼·奇普对锈笼说，“如果有人带着这样的女孩上门找你，帮我照顾她。”\n这名罗伊德·罗塞特生物实验室的保育员过去常在轻微的酒精作用下，自豪地说起公司是如何夺走那些土著赖以生存的雨林与水源，又如何在饥荒中仅仅花二十金券以及一些食物买下合格的阿达克利斯小孩。他还说，这些只值二十金券的小孩会被改造成“阿达克利斯战神”的复制品。他们最终会打败那些竞争对手，获得军方的订单，然后衣锦还乡……\n半年后，这个热忱的书呆子已是一个夜夜酩酊的酒鬼，总是绝望地抱怨实验有多么混乱：二期动物实验的一只羽兽逃了出去，一期和二期人体实验全部失败，所有实验体遭到销毁……最终他提到了实验体75号，这个四期人体实验中最不寻常的个体。\n实验体75号不仅没有双角，性格也与战争兵器毫不相关。哪怕经各种已验证有效的手段刺激至奄奄一息，她都丝毫没有展露出“战神”的特质。离奇的是，作为失败品的75号，带给年轻保育员的只是短暂的失落。很快，他不再酗酒，开始高兴地谈论实验体75号每日的生活，谈论他与保育员赛琳娜的美好未来，谈论他们可能会收养一个爱听公主故事的女儿，可能会一起去汐斯塔度假……一个错误的结果，却让迷失的灵魂寻见了正确的归途。\n然而，所有四期人体实验的“成功”实验体在某天服从训练时突然集体暴走，导致多名实验人员丧生。按规定流程，需要对该期实验体进行“人道”销毁。当晚，丹尼来到锈笼的酒馆，把实验体75号的照片交给了他。\n丹尼与那个女孩最终都没再光临过酒馆。\n实验室之后公示，丹尼和另一区的保育员赛琳娜已经在实验事故中“双双殒命”。\n六年过后，喧闹的酒客们变成了荒野猎人，酒馆里的精致菜肴换成了新鲜野味……本是随拓荒浪潮而建的酒馆，正在干涸的大地上与因患矿石病而被浪潮抛弃的拓荒者们艰难共存，就连生物实验室都已在软石区搁浅。\n此刻，锈笼望着不远处的女孩，又低头比对了手里的照片。虽不知何故长出了双角，但确是同一人无误。\n他看见了纯粹野性的狩猎，看见围绕着她而建立的食物链。他看文明的痕迹逐渐散去，荒野露出她本来的面目——已经重度感染的他毫无胜算。\n最后，锈笼放下了手中的猎弩。用尽最后的力气，为她送上自己囤积多年，荒野地的饯别礼。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
